**The Question**
> *If the sun sets over the ocean without anyone to watch it, is it still beautiful?*

**The Answer**

A ripple drifts across a pond.  
The Heron takes flight,  
unaware of the gravity holding the water in place.  
The water unaware of the moon,  
the moon unaware of the heron,  
the gravity unaware of the beauty,  
and the beauty unaware of everything  
other than  
itself.
